TEXT -1040 0 Left 2 !*\n.param Gfc=-13 ; magnitude at crossover\n.param  PS=-110 ; phase lag at crossover\n*\n* Enter Design Goals Information Here *\n*\n.param  fc=10k ; targeted crossover\n.param  PM=70 ; choose phase margin at crossover\n*\n* Enter the Values for Vout and Bridge Bias Current *\n*\n.param  Vout=5\n.param  Ibias=1m\n.param  Vref=2.5\n.param  Rlower=Vref/Ibias\n.param  Rupper=(Vout-Vref)/Ibias\n.param  kdiv=Rlower/(Rlower+Rupper)\n*\n* Capture the double zero position and one of the pole position *\n*\n.param  fz1=3k\n.param  fz2=3k\n.param  fp2=50k\n*\n* Do not edit the below lines *\n*\n.param  boost=PM-PS-90\n.param  G=(10**(-Gfc/20))/kdiv\n.param  fp1=fc/tan((atan(fc/fz1)+atan(fc/fz2)-atan(fc/fp2))-boost*pi/180) ; adjust second pole for targeted boost\n*\n.param  wz1={2*pi*fz1}\n.param  wz2={2*pi*fz2}\n.param  wp1={2*pi*fp1}\n.param  wp2={2*pi*fp2}\n*\n*\n.param  i={(1+fc**2/fp1**2)*(1+fc**2/fp2**2)}\n.param  j={(1+fz1**2/fc**2)*(1+fc**2/fz2**2)}\n.param  Wpi={sqrt(i/j)*G*fz1*2*pi}\n.param  z={(Wp1-Wz1)*(Wp1-Wz2)}\n.param  f={Wp1*Wz1+Wp1*Wz2-Wz1*Wz2}\n*\n.param  Td={z/(f*Wp1)}\n.param  N={((Wp1**2)/f)-1}\n.param  kp={(Wpi/Wz1)-(Wpi/Wp1)+(Wpi/Wz2)}\n.param  Ti={((Wz1+Wz2)/(Wz1*Wz2))-(1/Wp1)}\n.param  ki={kp/Ti}\n.param  kd={kp*Td}\n*\n*\n* Choose op amp characteristics *\n*\n.param AOL=100 ; open-loop gain in dB\n.param POLE=1G ; low-frequency pole\n.param VHIGH=5 ; upper output level\n.param VLOW=-5 ; lower output level\n*\n* Do not edit these lines *\n*\n.param GAIN={10**(AOL/20)}\n.param COL={1/(6.28*(GAIN/100u)*POLE)}\n.param ROL={GAIN/100u}\n*
TEXT 808 -24 Left 2 !.ac dec 100 10 100k
TEXT -104 1504 Left 2 ;This is a PID compensator built with op-amps. The op-amps will obviously\naffect the ac response of the compensator and you will see discrepancies\nbetween the realized functions which, in theory, shall be identical for:\n \nerr\nFilter_PID_FP2\nType 3\n \nTo observe an exact match, check the "Filtered PID - E sources" file.\n \nChristophe Basso - December 2024
